docs/DESIGN.md:113:   roster_version 1 fields; C3 writes its own data under `ext.c3` (priors, cost class). Until that wave lands, a sidecar
docs/DESIGN.md:114:   file holds the same data, because the current validator rejects unknown member keys.
docs/DESIGN.md:115: - Reward, defined once before any learning: per consultation, the coordinator's usefulness mark (yes 1, partly 0.5, no 0)
docs/DESIGN.md:116:   combined with the finding outcomes once they settle (verified +, rejected -), decayed by age, with an explicit rule for
docs/DESIGN.md:117:   the unrated (they count as missing, not as zero).
docs/DESIGN.md:118: - As built (M9, `docs/port/m9-spec.md`): router v1 keeps the plugin's seeded draw and replaces only the weight source,
docs/DESIGN.md:119:   `w = (yes + 0.5 partly + m*pi) / (n + m)`, of which the plugin's R15 is the case `pi = 0.5, m = 2`; with no priors
docs/DESIGN.md:120:   loaded every score and every byte of the ledger record equal the plugin's. Priors are a signed file (Ed25519, pinned
docs/DESIGN.md:121:   keys, fail closed), fetched at most once a day without any identifier and never followed across a redirect; a
docs/DESIGN.md:122:   published cell counts as evidence, so a fresh installation routes instead of falling back to roster order. What the
docs/DESIGN.md:123:   router used is recorded under one trailing `ext.c3` object of `panel.routing`; `c3 router replay` recomputes any
docs/DESIGN.md:124:   recorded draw, the plugin's included, from the ledger alone.

